# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
# File names carry no version hash, so a cached copy would go stale after a deploy and a visitor
# could run a new page with old scripts. "no-cache" makes the browser revalidate every file.
# An unchanged file costs one small 304 reply, because Pages sends an ETag.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
